OOC - A rare session with some cold beer tonight

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:OOC - nice. After my day at work I'm going with hot coffee

Asha Morrow:OOC hello hello

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:OOC: Let's get into it

![](https://files.d20.io/images/484317718/wanHEExdNPEx-WqTrBqG4Q/med.png?1776814791)

Saezo Ekron:Saezo walks back toward his Spark pumps without looking at you again. Business concluded. That's what that was.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The corridor outside is quieter than it should be. The gold light from the industrial glass dies somewhere around your boots. You are already turning back toward the lift. Back toward the Lone Star.

Nobody says much at first.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:"Kaelith, where do you think he's pumping all that Spark?" Lysa asks. Her eyes are fixed ahead on the industrial corridors and the random passing workers.

Asha Morrow:Asha has her own thoughts on that, _nowhere good_ or maybe Ternus since they seem to love the stuff. She waits for Kaelith to respond

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I wish I knew Lysa. But I it took a lot for me to blast those tubes behind him. He is making a fortune of the life force of mages and it makes me enraged."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:"What makes you so sure it's mages they're harvesting?"

Seraphine Morrow:"The last time our galaxy saw this type of magitech, it was Nefarius blood harvesting mages to power ships. I'd honestly find it difficult to believe this isn't just the same thing applied in a new way."

Asha Morrow:"And again, Ternus seems all the happy to use it."

Seraphine Morrow:Her face turns dark at that. "This time Ternus is the one supplying it, which seems worse."

Asha Morrow:"Joy."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I agree Seraphine. Where else are you gonna get that kind of force to power battleship cannons?"

Asha Morrow:"Growing up to find home has been the bad guys for..well at least my whole life, has been unpleasant."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:"This is what I was getting at earlier when I said it might be time for us to split our focus. We need to be in too many places. The Flame of Knowledge for one, but what about investigating what Spark is? Can we afford to wait?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Spark is widely used by the Terran's and i can't believe it all comes from Saezo. How many others could be producing it."

Asha Morrow:"I've bad experiences with splitting up, is all."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"Not from Saezo, he has just been positioning himself to control it. Make no mistake, we're importing it from Ternus."

She quickly adds, "I am starting to suspect that if you could pressure the right political figures, you would discover this trade moon deal has nothing to do with credits. There might be a 10-year required revenue clause for us, but I'm sure the primary clauses are about Spark. Oh to be a fly on the wall to read what was signed."

Asha Morrow:"Who would know about that? Maena?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"So where is Ternus getting it? Seraphine, did you ever stumble onto and secret slavery operations in your military service?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"The Inuran Matriarch would know, but getting an audience with her is not easy."

Seraphine Morrow:Seraphine adds to what Yraina is saying, "Or Rourke would know. Wonder if we could pressure him."

Asha Morrow:Asha pauses for the smallest moment before speaking, "Is that something you'd have a route to? Or know of?"

Seraphine Morrow:She responds to Kaelith. "The Ternus Confederacy operates largely on slave labor. We wipe the memories of criminals and conscript them. Citizens are largely coerced into it due to economic conditions. Do I know of secret military labs? Sure, there must be many of them. All over the galaxy. If Spark comes from somewhere, it's a state secret of the highest level. It is probably up there with protecting knowledge of Terra."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina goes still for a moment. The color drains out of her face just a little. When she answers, her voice is flat.

"I could get a message in front of her, yes. Maybe more than that if I pushed." She look away down the corridor, jaw tight. "Maena does not do casual family conversations and that's my way back in."

She seems to quickly shake it off in an attempt to put back on her professional pride as a Personal Shopper. "The Matriarch is not unfond of me at least."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"But mind wiping and conscripting Terran criminals does not get you enough magic to make Spark. They would need thousands upon thousands of innately magical beings."

Asha Morrow:Asha takes in a deep breath and tilts her head processing, "What exactly would we do if we knew, anyways?"

Seraphine Morrow:"With what we just saw, I'm not sure it's just mages. Even if we assume one mage could produce... maybe ten gallons of spark? You'd still need to be grinding up millions of mages every day to supply the economy. If Ternus could produce mages like that then we would have no problem winning our wars."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"It probably makes no difference at this point. It would only serve to figure out motivations, but motivations to what we still don't know."

Her comms ping suddenly and she checks her data slate, stops walking, and lifts it enough for the others to see.

**Commission complete. Item ready for collection.**

"It's ready, Kaelith."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith stops and glances at Yraina_ "Excellent news. We will have to grab it when we get the chance." _Kaelith states plainly, but is clearly as excited as a child on his birthday_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"No time like now."

Asha Morrow:"Surprised you would even consider waiting, let's go."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith smirks_ "Let's go then."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina turns without another word and takes you back off the polished paths, still in the orange service levels. The walk is familiar now: warmer air, uglier walls, thinner crowds. There is a feeling of important work being done in this place. At the end of the ribbed maintenance hall, the same dead little sign reads **Tain Salvage Calibration**. Inside is all heat and old magic.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith settles the skip in his stride as they approach the door and turns his demeanor to quiet and professional_

Asha Morrow:Asha is amused and doesn't mind showing it.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Orrel is waiting, the staff on a display rack beside him, waiting for Kaelith to step out and take it.

The staff is not pretty in the usual way. It is too precise for that, entirely Ternan in design and make. The artifact looks nothing like a usual tech mage's staff and more like the tool of a relic hunter.

The haft is long, dark, and clean-lined, with a matte metal frame that eats the workshop light instead of reflecting it. Calibrated rings sit along the length in hard, exact intervals. Each ring is etched with scale marks so small they look like scratches until you realize they are all intentional.

Down the center is a split channel of Reliquary Glass, clear enough that you can see the bench through it, except the view never quite lines up. Little pale smears move inside the glass when the staff turns. Not bubbles. Not dust. Something like mist caught in a sealed tube.

Bone of Xal runs beside that glass in a narrow black-white line. Near it, Blood of Shaya has been worked into green-gold capillaries under the frame. The life-patterns are there, but boxed in by Ternan geometry. Roots under glass.

The upper third is where it gets complicated. Small amber lenses catch under the surface. Thin crystal fins near the head shift with air that is not moving. Red-black stones sit deeper in the housing, quiet for now. The lower grip is layered shell and dark scale fitted tightly.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:There is no crown jewel or anything that looks like the business end of the staff. The top is an aperture made from nested rings, all of them almost aligned, less than a finger's width off.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486745157/MPhvk2tdGHp_zWT4r-C6tw/med.png?1778625234)

Orrel Tain:"You came back. Good. Close the door and let me show you what you bought."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:Lysa follows in but the others all opt to stay out.

Asha Morrow:Asha steps forward and finds a spot off to the side to give Kaelith the space to get closer while still having a good view. This is impressive work even to someone like Asha who knows little of artifacts.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith steps inside and closes the door once all who choose to join are inside_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:"I don't know what to say. I've never seen anything like this."

She folds her arms and is just utterly transfixed.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486745157/MPhvk2tdGHp_zWT4r-C6tw/med.png?1778625234)

Orrel Tain:"You did not ask me for a staff, not really. You wanted something that could survive Catalysts, take in every kind of magic, and wake up to stand beside you. So that was the goal when I made this. This is a person who is capable of surpassing you."

He steps aside and folds his arms, leaving Kaelith free to grab it if he wishes.

"Son, whatever you think you know about this world, you would consider it twice before you awaken this Eldimagus. You will never hear an artificer say this about their own work again in your life. Not Inura himself would build this, but I'm a shit-eating old man with a bone to pick so here you go."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:Lysa stares in quiet awe as she considers what she knows about Eldimagus and what she gathered based on his order. It's enough to make her paranoid for the moment.

Asha Morrow:Asha stares, impressed, but maybe not fully grasping the gravity of this moment. It is impressive work, beyond that she needs to see more to really understand.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren watches Kaelith carefully.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith looks at Orrel in amusement_ "An old man with a bone to pick you say? and i am to be the vessel by which this bone is picked I assume. Your creation is beautiful in many ways and stands apart from anything else that I have ever laid eyes on. I have touch greatness in the form of it's catalysts, but touching others with your creation exhilarates me." _Kaelith steps forward and examines the staff with his hands, lightly sliding his fingers around each intricate design aspect before taking hold and removing it from it's stand_ "Does the child have a name Orrel?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486745157/MPhvk2tdGHp_zWT4r-C6tw/med.png?1778625234)

Orrel Tain:"_Axiom_," he says.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:The staff settles into Kaelith's hands with a strange certainty, light in the grip but heavy like something magnetic. It does not feel asleep at all, just patient, like something holding perfectly still.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486745157/MPhvk2tdGHp_zWT4r-C6tw/med.png?1778625234)

Orrel Tain:"The order it should be catalyzed is Xal, Aashitak, Vaelith, Shaya, Wrathian, Fiscarra, Necrotis, Kee. Only one or two of those will be available to you, so you can substitute their corresponding element in place. Any water catalyst serves."

"if water is needed*"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Axiom. A strong name. I shall see to it that he is catalyzed in the order presented with as many of the named gods you prescribed."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486745157/MPhvk2tdGHp_zWT4r-C6tw/med.png?1778625234)

Orrel Tain:He nods to Kaelith.

"Get out of my shop then."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith nods in return and turns to exit the shop_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:Lysa follows without a word.

Asha Morrow:Asha snickers and follows Kaelith out.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:There's a general murmur among the group and a few congrats in various forms as Kaelith emerges with his new staff. All eyes are curious.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449929/F3ccik3dOgyO6n9WNHxu4A/med.png?1769556811)

Tamsin Vale:"For the first time in my life I'm a little jealous of something that isn't a rifle."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Xal was first on the list and we need to visit the Flame of Knowledge anyway, right?"

Asha Morrow:"Good point.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith smiles at Tamsin_ "I'm jealous of him too."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:"Convenient."

Asha Morrow:"Happy to head there first, dunno how long retrofitting the Lone Star is supposed to take, but we can come back if we need to."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"No need to leave and come back. We will finish the retrofit first."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Returning to the ship finally, everyone is gathered on the bridge. By the time you return, all of the equipment from Saezo has been delivered and Smoke is in the process of sorting it out and distributing it. The retrofit to the ship was performed so cleanly it borders on shocking. The Inurans' ability to reshape tech is unmatched, especially when coupled with the backing of real money, the speed of a trade moon, and the fact that Ternan tech borrows in large part from Inuran tech anyway.

A lot has changed. Consoles sit cleaner in their housings. Cbaling is gone from sight. The central projector has been rebuilt into something sharper and brighter emerging from the floor itself. Even the lighting is different, warmer in some places and clearer in others.

A few things are obvious right away. The command stations have been upgraded. The sensor and comms boards are faster and cleaner. The main displays are capable of holding a lot more information at once without looking cluttered. There is fresh armor worked into the bridge bulkheads in thin seamless layers, and the doors cycle faster when they open. It feels finished.

And more than that, the ship feels awake. It rumbles less, simply hums instead. The engines are the top of the line for Inuran spell drives. Much of the ship's material has been replaced by magical metamaterial, obvious both inside and out. There is much to discover, although for now it remains dormant and uncatalyzed.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449881/cL_uCLa-CsHARMqCKTqirg/med.png?1769556779)

Rho Anselm:Rho is busy gawking at his new seat and console at first.

Asha Morrow:Asha eats her words, looking shocked as she stares across at all the changes to the bridge. "Well, that was fast.." she mumbles

Seraphine Morrow:Seraphine just shakes her head slowly as she looks around the bridge. "We must be in the wrong ship, this makes no sense."

"We weren't gone that long."

Asha Morrow:"Makes some sense when you think of the inurans, I suppose."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith stumbles onto the bridge admiring Axiom, only to be met by the new beautiful bridge. He immediately heads to the rings to observe the changes to the matrixes_

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:She just smirks. "We have our ways."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:"What will you do then. You will seek out Xal now?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"That is what I prefer, but we are a crew with a Captain and I go where the ship goes."

Asha Morrow:"Its convenient for us, we need to head to the flame of knowledge to safely store the disk we recovered from Ternus anyways. Two birds. Plus I can now consider what to catalyze the Lone Star, Xal isn't a bad choice.."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:Just as Asha is speaking, the main screen alerts that a missive is coming in from Ternus. Specifically, Governor Rourke.

Asha Morrow:Asha answers, "What?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449741/4hyWxPbH2tEcZZNtLHiOSA/med.png?1769556706)

Governor Rourke:Rourke appears seated at his desk, suit clean, posture easy.

"Captain Morrow. Mage Voryn-Shai. I hope I'm not interrupting anything too important." He gives that half-smile. "I received an interesting request tied to an old freighter, which I'm happy to approve. More importantly, we are aware of what you are doing, but you've taken something of ours from Ternus. I'll cut to the chase, I want to know how serious it is."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith looks over to Asha to see her response_

Asha Morrow:Asha blinks for a few moments as she remembers what request they put in regarding the old freighter, she sighs and shoots a glance over at Kaelith. "Its fine." Asha is blunt.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith chimes in after seeing Asha look his way_ "You are aware of what we are doing? Ok well, then you know our work is important. I do however find it funny that you are now curious about something you left buried for millennia. But nonetheless it is a minor piece of information tied to **what we are doing**. As for my request, if you are happy to approve, please do and send the corresponding file our way if you would be so kind."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449741/4hyWxPbH2tEcZZNtLHiOSA/med.png?1769556706)

Governor Rourke:"Regardless of what you are doing, the file you took does not belong to you. You'll get your file when you return the disk to us."

Asha Morrow:"Cute. How about you tell us about where Spark comes from and we'll return the disk."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449741/4hyWxPbH2tEcZZNtLHiOSA/med.png?1769556706)

Governor Rourke:"And why would I discuss that with you?"

He pauses. "Does that disk have something to do with Spark?"

Asha Morrow:Asha considers something for a moment then proceeds, "You're kinda boring. I guess we'll make do without whatever Kaelith requested."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449741/4hyWxPbH2tEcZZNtLHiOSA/med.png?1769556706)

Governor Rourke:"Hold on-"

Asha Morrow:Asha looks over to her mother, "How did you tolerate dealing with these people?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449741/4hyWxPbH2tEcZZNtLHiOSA/med.png?1769556706)

Governor Rourke:"Look, all I can request at this point is that you keep me involved. If there is anything you decide you can surface publicly then I want you to contact me first."

Seraphine Morrow:"Insufferable pushovers, and Rourke is no better."

Asha Morrow:"When you decide you want to surface where spark comes from we'll come keep you involved, how's that sound? I swear Ternus is _dedicated_ to being on the wrong side of history. I can't imagine you're _ethically_ sourcing Spark." Asha's voice drips with sarcasm and disdain by the end.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449741/4hyWxPbH2tEcZZNtLHiOSA/med.png?1769556706)

Governor Rourke:The frustration is visible on his face as he leans forward on the desk. "Why the hell are you so interested in Spark?"

Asha Morrow:Asha's face contorts in momentary rage, "**Nothing** is free and whatever shortcut you're taking, whatever cheat you think you've found, you will not be the only one to pay the price when it comes back to haunt you."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449741/4hyWxPbH2tEcZZNtLHiOSA/med.png?1769556706)

Governor Rourke:"Let's say I can arrange that. What are you offering in return?"

Asha Morrow:"Amnesty."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449741/4hyWxPbH2tEcZZNtLHiOSA/med.png?1769556706)

Governor Rourke:He waves it away and ends the missive.

Asha Morrow:"That one dies for sure."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:She snickers with laughter.

Seraphine Morrow:"You hurt his ego, poor baby."

Asha Morrow:"I'm sure we'll find Spark is raw souls pulled from the afterlife or something and any ground he thought to stand on will crumble eventually. This whole thing is ridiculous. People actually believe nothing will ever come around to them." Asha pulls herself off the proverbial ledge and calms herself as she finds her seat in the captain's chair. "Lets head to Xal while I think about whether to catalyze our ship there or not. Yraina, do you know if this ship can handle multiple and different catalyzations or just one?"

(To Asha): +1 EXP

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:*Kaelith seems to visibly relax once the screen goes dark. That one need to die a slow ugly death. Arrogant prick! Guess we won't see that freighter file after all."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:"It was outfit to accept just one it seems."

"So choose wisely."

Asha Morrow:"Xal seems like the obvious, if a bit.._boring_ choice. We are essentially his champions at this point."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/473449881/cL_uCLa-CsHARMqCKTqirg/med.png?1769556779)

Rho Anselm:"Suppose you could take it back to the source. Aashitak."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:"I would save it."

Asha Morrow:"Suppose so. Kaelith will need to catalyze Axiom at Aashitak eventually."

"Save it? For who?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:OOC - can you make me a note sheet please

![](https://files.d20.io/images/478181285/NyR01STWeLZW7Jx5gInttg/med.png?1772584898)

Nyrix:OOC - Sure one sec

"Hmm..." she thinks and then slowly crosses her arms. "You have your map. You can always catalyze it, so wait until you need it most, or until the fates show you the way."

"Trust in who is the better question to ask yourself."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/475374291/w5WLbKJjcQMYwhHAmAq-jg/med.png?1770766669)

Lysa Vorren:"I don't know that we have the luxury to wait around. An Eldimagus spellship would be... well.." she stares off to the side. "Pretty useful."

