Rho Anselm:Rho is checking the instruments and confirms they are in fact in the system of Xal. The look on his face is distant for a moment at that. The fact that such power exists is ridiculous to him. But it is replaced by an appreciation for what he has here. A purpose, a crew, and a chance.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"This staff holds pieces of every element and holds the potential to eclipse my power quickly after is awakens. We will all have to wait and see just what kind of weapon he will become. For now he is my spell focus and my sleeping companion."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/486756473/LrNCmB87c4vuW1tupLerqw/med.png?1778631209)

Yraina:Yraina is standing with an unreadable look on her face as she watches this. Her eyes are transfixed on Aran, but she studies the rest of the room and the others as they speak and whisper. She is otherwise still, invisibly tensed waiting to react to nothing.

Asha Morrow:"Yeah well, try to be a good..."father" or maybe "friend" is more appropriate, to Axiom. That's what's important Kaelith. Well adjusted gods and artifacts only please."

Xal Aran:"I won't bother prying for details on who made it or why you have it, but I like it. I won't stop you from catalyzing it. You are free to do as you wish so long as you seek Ikadra's blessing first. Conveniently, Voria is visiting. She's out by the catalyst now."

Asha Morrow:"Ideal."

Xal Aran:"Onto the next point. The Flame of Knowledge is not an ideal place to be visiting. It's dangerous. Is all you want for us to store something on it?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Of course Aran."

Asha Morrow:Asha pulls out the disk, "Just this. Some.._old_ knowledge, befitting the Flame of Knowledge as its resting place."

Xal Aran:He offers his hand to take it if she wishes to drop it in. "The best place to store something old and worth forgetting is the Flame. I will see to it that nobody ever finds it, unless you need it back one day. It is well protected."

Asha Morrow:Asha places it in his hand and nods, "Cool. Fuck Ternus by the way." she adds, bluntly.

Xal Aran:He examines it for just a moment in the air between his fingers and then asks. "Old Ternus technology?"

Asha Morrow:"Indeed. They are a planet of secrets and _stupid_ short sighted decisions."

Xal Aran:He sighs. "I agree. I don't think they are capable of carrying on without constantly finding a war to fight. But what are we to do? I still don't believe they have forgiven Voria for being framed for destroying Colony-3."

"Their entire society is built around something I don't understand."

Asha Morrow:"Whatever Spark is, they're in deep and still digging."

Xal Aran:"Spark is potentially the largest threat we've faced since Nefarius. We should speak more about this, but you have Nara to confront."

Asha Morrow:"Indeed, and Kaelith is eager to catalyze Axiom the first time I am sure. Let's do this."

Xal Aran:He thinks for a moment and then decides something. "I'm not going to make you walk there. She's just trying to work something out, so how about I make it easy and take two of you over to her directly?"

Asha Morrow:"I'm good for it."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"I'm down"

Xal Aran:Aran claps the two of you on the shoulder each and within the blink of an eye you are just seamlessly on the skull of Xal outside. If your power armor was not helmet up already, then it doesn't seem to matter. Your atmosphere is maintained here.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/465566247/kx383qakTiwpkERKIActNg/med.webp?1764114136)

Narrator:This is some unknown distance out onto the surface of the Skull of Xal, not inside the eye socket where most affairs are conducted, and where the easiest entrance to the catalyst is. Nara is hard casting something complex at the edge of a long drop-off, a cliff of bone. Below is a canyon leading to a small structure about a kilometer away. The area between is slowly being crushed by the weight of intense gravity, strong enough to cause the bone surface of the skull to crack as she repeats the spell again.

Asha Morrow:Asha stands and watches quietly for the moment.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith watches intently and does not make a sound_

Xal Nara:Nara stops a few iterations in after they arrive and turns around to face the group. She looks surprised at first, as though she was genuinely not aware anyone was here. The annoyance is obvious in her tail and her expression as she digs her staff into the ground and stands up straight. "Really? Do _you_ think it's good to bring visitors in while I'm literally casting the traps for our vault?"

Xal Aran:"Oh come on, they are friends."

Xal Nara:"Dear, we'll talk later."

Asha Morrow:Asha opens her mouth as if to ask about the vault, then thinks better of it.

Xal Aran:He disappears and leaves you to it.

Xal Nara:"I'm sorry, I didn't mean to be so rude."

Asha Morrow:Asha handwaves it away, "So..we spent some time here last time. Some of us, myself included, trained with you. Did you not think to mention you were responsible for planting the catalyst map on the freighter?"

Xal Nara:Nara stares a moment to long and then nods in acceptance at what Asha just said. "I know and you have a right to be upset with me."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:_Kaelith looks a little surprised at the tone Asha started the conversation with_

Asha Morrow:Asha just pauses and stares, then holds her hands out, "Okay, keep talking."

Xal Nara:She tilts her head slightly at that and her tail slowly comes back to life. "It was not originally my job, but thanks to Necrotis we're now responsible for the Flame. Do you know what the Web of Divinity is?"

Asha Morrow:"No, and I haven't met Necrotis yet."

Xal Nara:"You never will meet Necrotis, thankfully. She is dead. And may Spirit magic never return. I'm tired of it. Her, Krox, every time someone rises up with Spirit it becomes worse than war, just nightmares."

Asha Morrow:Asha's eyes dart to Kaelith, thinking of Tain's order for catalyzing Axiom, but she says nothing and returns to stare back at Nara. "Well, Spirit magic was used on the freighter. Though I don't know how long ago exactly that was."

Xal Nara:A look of immediate interest flashes through her eyes at that. "What kind of Spirit magic?"

Asha Morrow:"Uhh,-" she turns to Kaelith then back, "I don't know enough of Spirit magic to say, but the captain was enthralled in some way, is my understanding at least."

Xal Nara:"A binding then. Do you know who did it?"

She glances at both of them.

Asha Morrow:Asha sucks air between her teeth, "Well..signs point to inurans, the Maena family we think."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Yes the Captain of the ship was guided by a Spirit mage to follow a predetermined course of action and lead the vessel into an ambush I guess you would call it."

Xal Nara:"_Spirit_ again," she scowls.

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Yes, it appears the Maena family were the responsible party."

Xal Nara:"To answer your other question, the Flame holds the Web. It is... was made by..." she trails off and her gaze drifts off for a second before snapping back. "You can find her in..." she trails off again.

Again a second later she snaps back to it and asks, "Hopefully you see what I mean. The only way I know how to describe it without triggering it is to tell you that divination itself was made by the same thing. There is a way to access it... if you are following so far."

Asha Morrow:"Uhhh, kind of? Maybe?" her face scrunches up, "The web is why you dropped the map at the freighter?"

Xal Nara:"The one who interfaces with the web warned us that the web of possible futures was rapidly collapsing. In an increasing number of timelines, you all die violently on that trade moon."

"In one of the few where you survive, we drop the scale decades ago."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Are there any pieces of Necrotis left to Catalyze?"

Asha Morrow:"Who..what...kills us on the trade moon?"

Xal Nara:"Necrotis... what.."

Asha Morrow:Asha looks at Kaelith like he is insane to ask this.

Xal Nara:"What kind of dumbass question is that, why would you want to catalyze with Necrotis?"

She looks infuriated at this.

