Xal Nara:She looks suspicious at this but buys it. "Her _ship_ is held in our space here, yes. There's plenty left but we would know if anyone even came close to it."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Excellent then it is safe under your lock and key."

Xal Nara:"Yes, the Maker's Wrath is secure."

OOC: Lore-note, Maker = Inura

Asha Morrow:Asha looks tense and still shocked but she tries to move on, "So..what were our deaths like in those possible futures. Why did we die on the trade moon? Why did you care to prevent it?"

Xal Nara:She looks hesitant to speak at this point, perhaps because of the question or the answer it's not clear.

"What do you think Magic is?"

Asha Morrow:Asha stares, "There are a million ways to answer that question."

Xal Nara:"Exactly, I don't expect you to pick one. But we all get it from where?"

Asha Morrow:"From others. Gods, or.." she looks for the word, "Titans even. Some source that already had it."

Xal Nara:"Right, we're all eating the corpse of something older or larger. Everyone you know now, even Virkonna herself who I give a 50/50 at best of killing us in a fight. She was once a hatchling eating Xal of all things. And Xal just happened to be a mage who was there with the Titans and helped to design part of the Great Cycle. But in Xal's world he was originally just a person. They chose to make our universe, but no matter what their intention was... originally there must have been a betrayal. We understand that to be Krox, but behind him was truly Nefarius."

Asha Morrow:Asha nods along, surprisingly following this and waiting for how this connects.

Xal Nara:She goes on, "In a sense at least the cycle they envisioned was maintained because it was life eating life, returning even the gods themselves to the Spirit world. You know, sometimes I think maybe that was the whole point. They needed to be able to be consumed by it too. But now Ternus is fucking it up."

Asha Morrow:"How? Spark?"

Xal Nara:"Right, where's the mage? How the fuck do you bottle magic?"

She gestures at that.

Asha Morrow:"What is Spark?"

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"So, did you know it would be us that found the map?"

Xal Nara:"From what we can tell, it's raw magic."

Asha Morrow:"How?"

Xal Nara:"You can just use it."

She shrugs and looks exasperated at that.

"I wish I knew."

Asha Morrow:"We are going to find out that Spark comes from some fucked up process and it is going to make me rage. The tension is palpable."

Xal Nara:"Kaelith, I did. We have been watching this unfold ever since Necrotis died, and we arranged to ensure you both ended up on that salvage job and that you would get the scale."

She points to Nara and just says, "Exactly."

"Trust me, I used to be one of their own fucked up experiments."

"They have labs everywhere."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Why us Nara? What did you see that made you pick us?"

Xal Nara:She continues without waiting to explain, "In every timeline where you die, something happens. The souls of every human on Ternus are ripped into the Trade Moon and a new God is born, but without living first. What follows is the end of possibility, all divination leads to the end. It is a hole in the web, which is why it was brought to our attention. A hole should not be possible."

"But if you survive, then the web reopens back into all of the possible futures, so we had no choice but to manipulate you into this position."

Asha Morrow:"The..Spark. We met an Inuran merchant who is storing..._industrial_ amounts of it. He can't be the only one."

Xal Nara:"Yeah..." she replies.

Asha Morrow:"All that raw magic and the trade moon..I don't know how to connect ripping the souls of all of Ternus away, but somehow it must."

"Tsk. I fucking knew we were going to have to kill a whole lot of people."

Asha looks annoyed now, "People are so fucking stupid."

Xal Nara:"They're honestly just the worst, it's so dumb."

"We suck."

"What did you find on that disk anyway?"

Asha Morrow:"Terra. Or rather, what happened to it."

Xal Nara:Her eyes widen at that and she takes a step back.

"Excuse me?"

Asha Morrow:"Yeah and they did some fucking _weird_ magic to it."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"It is a piece of the mystery of the Hand of Errata that they missed destroying."

Xal Nara:"We've known for a while that there is another player, but can't see who it is. Maybe this is the lead we're looking for."

Nara paces slowly as she thinks before finally speaking again. "What I don't understand is why the incident hasn't happened yet. It's impossible to say how much time you have, so we need to trust each other and hope for the best at this point."

Asha Morrow:"It..would've already happened by now?"

Xal Nara:"Shortly after you first arrived at the moon, yes."

Asha Morrow:"Huh.. how's it feel to bed dead in another timeline Kaelith?"

Xal Nara:"Almost all of them."

Asha Morrow:"Oh."

'Well when you put it like that I kinda feel like I should be dead and that's not a great feeling.."

Asha rubs her face.

Xal Nara:"Right, we are a speck floating in the abyss right now."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Perhaps we need to peer into the past and see what changed. You have never been able to see the cause of the catastrophe?"

Xal Nara:"The cause is always different, seemingly random. But when you take the freighter and try to dock it, and run away with the scale, it doesn't happen."

"Or at least it's delayed."

Asha Morrow:"In the realities where we live, does the freighter always blow up at the dock?"

Xal Nara:"Sure does, why?"

Asha Morrow:"Well thats a consistent detail that wouldn't happen otherwise, I'm looking for any reason why the death of Ternus is delayed. Maybe wrecking the dock delayed the flow of Spark in some way."

Xal Nara:"I suppose it could have slowed down some key shipments, maybe right place right time to prevent a wrong place wrong time, but it's a long shot."

"Was there anything unusual about the ship?"

Asha Morrow:"I just don't think there was anything we've done that would have delayed it so far. We haven't wrecked Spark production or ruined supply on the Trade Moon."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Perhaps Joren was not who was supposed to trigger the event at the dock. Perhaps someone with more power and magic was supposed to be the one."

Xal Nara:"You think the spell misfired? Only partially took effect."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"It's possible. As far as know, Joren had no laten magic. Perhaps the spell was designed to absorb the additional power of a mage before triggering."

Xal Nara:"You were a capable mage at the time, yes?"

Asha Morrow:"Indeed, Kaelith has always been strong."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"At that point I possessed Void and fire. The perfect trigger for the event."

Xal Nara:"Then we could ask the web what would have happened if you had been the one to activate it."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"That would certainly be helpful. Can anyone use the web?"

Xal Nara:"No, a single encounter with the web inflicts permanent insanity. It can be resisted for a while but it will eventually consume you. But you can speak to the one who does use it."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Oh, just permanent insanity. Great awesome. Sign me up." _Kaelith laughs_

Asha Morrow:"Uh, and the one who does use it is..insane?"

Xal Nara:She grins at that.

"We all have sacrifices to make. Some guy handles the web for us. I honestly don't know all that much about his story but he has been there a while. It's hard to call him a guy, he's just a lot of spiders. Like more than you think."

![](https://files.d20.io/images/463501989/uffoiECHgg_FePKmfVj4AA/med.webp?1762706719)

Kaelith Voryn-Shai:"Shall we go visit him and ask the million dollar question?"

